{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And if it is an unclean beast, etc.</b> This verse is not spoken of the firstborn — for one cannot say of a firstborn unclean beast 'and redeem it at your valuation' — and this is not the donkey, for the redemption of the firstborn donkey is only a lamb, and it is a gift to the priest, not for consecration. Rather, the verse is spoken of consecration: the verse above spoke of redeeming a clean beast that had a blemish, and here it speaks of one who consecrates an unclean beast for the upkeep of the Temple." "<b>And redeem it at your valuation.</b> According to whatever value the priest sets for it." "<b>And if it is not redeemed.</b> By the owners." "<b>And it is sold at your valuation.</b> To others."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:59.654504158Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}